    "turn_text": "assistant, Shava Bruce, and asking. In August of that year, 1997, 60 minutes interviewed myself and General Levitt. The lead story in September of 1997 on 60 minutes was the public announcement that General Levitt said Russia could not account for approximately 80 small nuclear devices just like this one. But then the story gets worse. Because the next day, the Russian Foreign Ministry called Levitt a liar. They said he would not have been able to know this information and he's only looking to run for office again and they trash Levitt. But the day after was worse because the media asked our spokespeople and the press conference was held and the Clinton administration publicly said to the American people, we have no reason to doubt the word of the Russian government. So then I had the Russian government and our government denying that this was a problem. So in October of that year, I brought over a top Russian academician who runs the top environmental center in Russia. His name is Dr. Alexa Yablakov, and I had him testify before Congress. And he set on the record what Lib had said is true. He said, I have colleagues in the Academy of Sciences who worked on this technology, who built these devices, and you, America, must help us find them, because otherwise we're all going to be threatened by them. In December of that year, I had a face-to-face meeting with the Russian Defense Minister. In his office in Moscow, his name was Marshal Sergeyev. And I said, General Sergeyev, he and I had gotten along. I said, you want me to help you with the problems in your military? You want me to help you with housing for your troops? Yes, Congress, and I need your help. I said that you have to help me. I need to know the truth. Levitt told me last May that he couldn't account for any devices. Your public, your foreign ministry has said you never built these devices. So, General Sergei, I need to know the truth. Did you build them or not? in december of that year marshal sir gave look be in the eye and said yes congressman we did build these devices and i assure you that by the year two thousand we will have them all accounted for that was in nineteen ninety seven after the russian government and our government",
